  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Complex Power Series and Analyticity [S+N]\n\nPower series in $\\mathbb{C}$ are like real ones, but with disks instead of intervals. A series $\\sum c_n (z - z_0)^n$ has a **radius of convergence** $R$ (Cauchy-Hadamard, same formula as in real analysis):\n\n$$\\frac{1}{R} = \\limsup_{n \\to \\infty} |c_n|^{1/n}.$$\n\nInside $\\{|z - z_0| < R\\}$ — the **disk of convergence** — the series converges absolutely. Outside, it diverges. On the boundary, behaviour is delicate.\n\nA function holomorphic on a disk equals its Taylor series there. We saw the hint in real analysis: $1/(1+x^2)$ has Taylor radius 1 because the complex singularities at $\\pm i$ are at distance 1. Now we can finally explain that.\n\nThis notebook formalises: holomorphic ⇔ analytic on disks, with all the consequences.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "load(\"numerics\")$\nload(\"ax-plots\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 11,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Geometric series in $\\mathbb{C}$\n\n$\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty z^n = 1/(1 - z)$ for $|z| < 1$. The disk of convergence is the open unit disk; on the boundary $|z| = 1$ the series diverges (the terms don't go to zero).\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "z_test : 0.5 + 0.3 * %i$\nabs_z : float(cabs(z_test))$\nprint(\"z =\", z_test, \"  |z| =\", abs_z)$\nN : 50$\nrunning : 0.0 + 0.0*%i$\nfor n : 0 thru N do running : running + z_test^n$\nprint(\"Σ z^n (N=\", N, \"):\", expand(running))$\nprint(\"1/(1-z):\", expand(1/(1 - z_test)))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 12,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "z = 0.3*%i+0.5   |z| = 0.58309518948453\nΣ z^n (N= 50 ): 0.8823529411761379*%i+1.4705882352960256\n1/(1-z): 1/(0.5-0.3*%i)"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Visualising the disk of convergence\n\nThe set of $z$ where partial sums of a power series stay bounded forms a *disk* (in $\\mathbb{C}$), not an arbitrary set. Plot the values of $|S_N(z)|$ for the geometric series at $N = 50$ as a heatmap-like surface — bounded inside the unit disk, blowing up near $|z| = 1$, hopelessly large outside.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* The geometric series converges to 1/(1 - z) inside |z| < 1 — plot the\n   limit's modulus, clamped to keep the figure bounded near the boundary. */\ngeom_mod : cabs(1 / (1 - (x + y*%i)))$\nax_draw3d(\n  explicit(min(geom_mod, 5), x, -1.4, 1.4, y, -1.4, 1.4),\n  title=\"|1/(1-z)| — finite inside |z|<1, blows up at the boundary\",\n  xlabel=\"Re z\", ylabel=\"Im z\", zlabel=\"|f|\",\n  colorscale=\"Hot\"\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 13,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
